1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,000
Hi, and welcome to the Warp Drive demo.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
This is my Factorio save,
with one space platform.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
It's halfway to the Shattered Planet,
on its way back.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,900
It's stuck at 20 km/s:
too many asteroids.

5
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,700
Here is the Warp Drive.

6
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:18,000
Not ready yet:
warp needs 50 km/s.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,500
For better timing, I let the
circuit network engage the drive.

8
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,000
The condition is always true…

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,500
…so the drive engages as soon as
every requirement is met.

10
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,400
Only speed is missing.

11
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,500
This circuit caps
the platform's speed.

12
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,900
I raise the cap to 55 km/s.

13
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,200
Back to the drive.

14
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:46,500
It's already charging
for warp entry.

15
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:49,500
Jump energy depends
on the platform's mass.

16
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,000
Let's zoom out to watch the jump.

17
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,200
Still in normal space,
surrounded by asteroids…

18
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,500
…jump!

19
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:01,000
The ship has breached
the subspace barrier.

20
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,700
No asteroids here:
it travels in complete safety.

21
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,000
Let's check the drive.

22
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The dialog shows the warp level
and the effective speed.

23
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,500
The game's own UI still shows
only the engine speed.

24
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:20,200
That's a game limitation:
a mod can't change it.

25
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:23,000
Let's go faster.

26
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,700
I raise the speed cap
in the circuit again.

27
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:32,000
Engine speed feeds
the warp multiplier.

28
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The warp level climbs…

29
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,200
…and effective speed grows
much faster than engine speed.

30
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:45,000
Now the space map.

31
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,500
While in warp, the platform's name
gets a cyan WARP suffix.

32
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:54,000
It moves so fast you can see it
with the naked eye.

33
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Even on the full route view.

34
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Next: leaving warp.

35
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,300
Warp is still active.

36
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:07,700
Before leaving, you usually
want to slow down.

37
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:12,500
So I lower the speed cap
below 50 km/s.

38
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:16,500
Leave at full speed, and the ship lands
in normal space at a very high speed…

39
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:20,400
…right into the asteroids.

40
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,700
Wait, or press Disengage.

41
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:25,400
Disengaged.

42
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:30,700
Back in normal space.

43
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:34,500
And the asteroids appear again.

44
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:39,900
That's why you slow down
before you drop out of warp.

45
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,200
The drive is charging again!

46
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,500
My circuit wobbled
above 50.

47
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:46,200
It dropped back,
so no jump.

48
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:49,500
Let's push the speed
back above 50 km/s.

49
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:53,400
Asteroids hit hard at this speed…

50
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:57,000
…while the drive charges
for the jump.

51
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,200
Almost there…

52
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,500
Jump!

53
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:06,000
Yes! The ship made it.

54
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Back in subspace,
but not unscathed.

55
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,000
The corner turrets were destroyed.

56
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,700
But the warp holds,
and the ship is safe.

57
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:22,500
That's the Warp Drive: engaged,
disengaged, and engaged again.

58
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:27,500
Thanks for watching!
